cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SPARSH, please cite the article that describes it. Until it is published, please cite this software."
title: "SPARSH: Subtype Prediction via Adaptive Recognition from Sparse Hematological data"
abstract: "SPARSH uses a neural network trained on Illumina methylation arrays to classify acute leukemia from the sparse CpG methylation calls of a low-pass nanopore genome run. From the same reads it estimates copy number along the genome and writes it as a karyotype, and it puts both into a report for each case."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ACTREC, Tata Memorial Centre"
    city: "Navi Mumbai"
    country: IN
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/patkarlab/sparsh"
keywords:
  - acute leukemia
  - DNA methylation
  - nanopore sequencing
  - classification
  - copy number
